{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "NMR", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of this peptide shows 46.7% similarity to EntEJ97. Mol formula: C218H325N51O51S2; Mol Wt 4564.386. GRAVY= -0.7; Wimley-White whole-residue hydrophobicity of the peptide: 2.54 kcal/mol. Mol ex. coeff. 15632.5. Activity: Highly Potent against E. faecium. (?) rseP Expression in S. pneumoniae confers sensitivity to EntEJ97/EntK1. Structure: 3D structure was determined in 50% TFE by NMR: A central helix with both termini disordered. Simialr to LsbB, this peptide targets the receptor RseP.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "28515717", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Microbiol. 2017 May 3;8:774. doi: 10.3389/fmicb.2017.00774. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02914", "source_id": "AP02914", "source_numeric_id": "02914", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02914", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "The Leaderless Bacteriocin Enterocin K1 Is Highly Potent against Enterococcus faecium: A Study on Structure, Target Spectrum and Receptor", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
